## Theorem

The canonical rational function `det J(a)` is not identically zero. Indeed,
G3CE gives the exact reduction

```text
det J(0) = 4 mod 11.
```

The unit reduction proves that the corresponding characteristic-zero value is
nonzero. Hence all zeros and poles of `det J(a)` are algebraic complex numbers
in every Archimedean embedding of `k`.

G3BK likewise proves that all parent H20, H11 and H02 chart poles are
algebraic. G3BJ selects

```text
a(t)=1-t+i*pi*t*(1-t),  0<=t<=1,
```

and proves that every value with `0<t<1` is transcendental. Therefore no
interior path point is a zero or pole of `J`, or a pole of a parent chart.
The B89 endpoint `t=1`, `a=0` is covered by the G3CE unit certificate. At the
other endpoint, G3BN and G3BR prove that the exact same selected H11 and H02
parent charts are units over `Q(gamma)`, using determinants `276` and `419`
modulo `21817`. Thus no parent-chart transition remains anywhere on the path.

Consequently one Schur gauge covers the complete domain

```text
0<t<=1.
```

On this domain the following are uniquely defined in `k(a)`:

```text
S_C(a)   = A(a)-U(a)J(a)^-1L(a),
b_eff(a) =       -U(a)J(a)^-1b_lower(a).
```

The corresponding static affine obstruction matrix has dimension 249. For the
algebraic equation `K_C(a)z+b_C(a)=0`, the lower 1,261 coordinates are
recovered by

```text
z_lower=-J(a)^-1(L(a)z_H20+b_lower(a)).
```

Only invertibility of the derived 1,261-square lower block `J(1)` at the
initial G3BI endpoint remains undecided. If it vanishes, a limiting Schur
initializer is required even though all parent residue charts are valid.

## Proof boundary

This theorem removes an interior atlas search for the **static obstruction
problem**. It does not emit the rational
coefficients of `K_C(a)`, `J(a)`, `S_C(a)` or `b_eff(a)`; it proves that the
already selected algebraic construction defines them and that the Schur
denominators cannot vanish on the open path.

It also does not promote the terminal `GF(11)` rank-247 Schur defect to
characteristic zero. Rank may jump after reduction even though the lower block
is a unit. Most importantly, static row elimination does not reduce a
connection ODE. Such a reduction requires a differentiable invariant graph
and its Riccati identities, including derivative terms. Until that theorem is
proved, transport remains rank 1,510. No integral B89 marking, 248-row readout
or `beta_C` value is inferred.

## Consequence

The remaining analytic work is no longer a general multi-chart problem. It is
now exactly:

1. evaluate `det J(1)` or construct its limiting condition at `a=1`;
2. compute the derivative/Riccati identities for the variable Schur graph;
